In the second age, torches were brought to the deep.
The flickering light revealed inscriptions
on every wall, written in a language
that few could read and fewer still could speak.

The dungeon masters built forges in the lower levels,
crafting weapons and tools from ore found
in the veins of rock that ran through the stone.

Great feasts were held in the main hall,
where warriors and scholars gathered as equals.

The second rune was forged in fire,
tempered by the heat of the deepest forge.

DECOY MARKING: NOT A REAL RUNE

The blacksmiths were said to have created
a masterwork blade, but its location
was lost when the forges went cold.

RUNE: FLAME

The flame rune burned with an inner light
that could not be extinguished by water or wind.
Those who carried it could see in the deepest dark
and feel warmth even in the coldest chamber.

Many adventurers sought the flame rune,
but most were turned away by the guardians
who watched over the archives day and night.

The old texts speak of a third rune,
hidden in the most obscure corner of the library,
waiting for one clever enough to find it.
